# 🚀 Node.js Basics — HTTP & Express

A hands-on learning repo covering **Node.js fundamentals** — starting with the native `http` module and then moving to **Express**, showing *when and why to use each*.

This repo is designed like interview-ready notes + working mini-projects

---

## ✨ What you’ll learn

### 🔹 HTTP (Built-in Node)
- Creating a basic HTTP server  
- Request & Response lifecycle  
- Routing manually  
- Parsing JSON & Query Params  
- Why HTTP becomes hard as apps grow

### 🔹 Express
- Creating an Express server  
- Middleware (logging, parsing, auth basics)  
- Routing the right way  
- Error handling  
- When Express saves time (and when raw HTTP is fine)

---

